---
import Landing from "../../layouts/Landing.astro";
import Footer from "../../features/navigation/components/Footer.astro";
import SiteHeader from "../../features/navigation/components/SiteHeader.astro";
import { ShieldCheck, LockKey, Key, Database, Cpu, FileText } from "@phosphor-icons/react";

const locale = "en";
---

<Landing locale={locale} title="Security — Qably" description="What Qably protects, what it does with test files, and which data reaches third parties. It describes only what the product does today.">
  <SiteHeader locale={locale} altHref="/security" />

  {/* Main Security Content */}
  <main id="main-content" class="max-w-4xl mx-auto px-6 pt-28 pb-16 flex-grow font-sans text-zinc-300 leading-relaxed space-y-12">
    <header class="space-y-3 pb-8 border-b border-white/[0.08]">
      <p class="text-xs text-zinc-500 uppercase tracking-wider font-medium">What the product does today</p>
      <h1 class="text-3xl sm:text-5xl font-semibold tracking-tight text-white">Security</h1>
      <p class="text-base text-zinc-400">
        What Qably protects, how it protects it, and which data reaches third parties. This page describes only what the product does today.
      </p>
    </header>

    {/* Security Pillar Cards */}
    <div class="grid grid-cols-1 md:grid-cols-3 gap-4">
      <div class="p-5 rounded-xl border border-white/[0.08] bg-zinc-950 space-y-2">
        <LockKey size={22} className="text-white" weight="bold" />
        <h3 class="text-sm font-semibold text-white">Encrypted secrets</h3>
        <p class="text-xs text-zinc-400 leading-relaxed">
          Webhook secrets, repository access tokens, and Slack and Discord webhook URLs are encrypted with AES-256-GCM before they are stored.
        </p>
      </div>

      <div class="p-5 rounded-xl border border-white/[0.08] bg-zinc-950 space-y-2">
        <ShieldCheck size={22} className="text-white" weight="bold" />
        <h3 class="text-sm font-semibold text-white">Human review</h3>
        <p class="text-xs text-zinc-400 leading-relaxed">
          New cases proposed by the AI wait in a review inbox and enter the catalog only when a person approves them.
        </p>
      </div>

      <div class="p-5 rounded-xl border border-white/[0.08] bg-zinc-950 space-y-2">
        <Key size={22} className="text-white" weight="bold" />
        <h3 class="text-sm font-semibold text-white">Project-scoped API keys</h3>
        <p class="text-xs text-zinc-400 leading-relaxed">
          Each key belongs to one project, is shown only once, and is stored only as a SHA-256 hash. An owner or an admin can revoke it.
        </p>
      </div>
    </div>

    <section class="space-y-4">
      <h2 class="text-xl font-semibold text-white tracking-tight">1. Access and roles</h2>
      <p class="text-sm text-zinc-400">
        Each organization has three roles: <code class="text-white font-mono">owner</code>, <code class="text-white font-mono">admin</code>, and <code class="text-white font-mono">member</code>. Only owners and admins can create and revoke API keys, manage repository connections, and configure notification webhooks. An API key identifies one project: the results it sends are recorded in that project. A revoked key is no longer accepted.
      </p>
    </section>

    <section class="space-y-4">
      <h2 class="text-xl font-semibold text-white tracking-tight">2. Connections and webhooks</h2>
      <p class="text-sm text-zinc-400">
        Communication with the application and the API uses HTTPS, and in production session cookies are issued with the Secure attribute. Events that GitHub sends through a webhook are accepted only when their HMAC-SHA256 signature matches the connection's secret. That secret can be rotated from the application.
      </p>
    </section>

    <section class="space-y-4">
      <h2 class="text-xl font-semibold text-white tracking-tight">3. Test files and the AI provider</h2>
      <p class="text-sm text-zinc-400">
        Qably does not clone repositories. To document a test file, it reads that file from the connected GitHub repository and sends its content to Google Gemini, up to a character limit that depends on the plan. Conversations with Aeris send the same provider the message, the history, the project context and, when a case is consulted, fragments of its test file. For each proposal, Qably stores the file path and a short quote of its code as evidence.
      </p>
    </section>

    <section class="space-y-4">
      <h2 class="text-xl font-semibold text-white tracking-tight">4. Review decisions and API keys</h2>
      <p class="text-sm text-zinc-400">
        Each review decision, whether an approval or a rejection, records who made it, when, and the comment, if there is one. For each API key, Qably stores the creation date, the last-use date and, if it is revoked, the revocation date.
      </p>
    </section>
  </main>

  <Footer locale={locale} />
</Landing>
